---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ClosingBand from '../../components/ClosingBand.astro';
import MirrorWording from '../../components/MirrorWording.astro';

const wordings = [
  {
    label: 'Mirror glass',
    steps: [
      ['Component', 'Glass only. The housing and mount can stay on the door.'],
      ['Position', 'Left exterior mirror, as viewed facing forward.'],
      ['Equipment', 'Match the heater connections and backing plate to the original glass.'],
    ],
    example:
      'Can you quote the left mirror glass on its own? The heater terminals are on the back. ' +
      'We’re keeping the housing and mount. Does the replacement come with the backing plate?',
  },
  {
    label: 'Complete assembly',
    steps: [
      ['Component', 'Complete mirror, including its housing and mount.'],
      ['Position', 'Left side. The hinge is broken.'],
      [
        'Equipment',
        'Check power adjustment and folding, glass heating and any fitted indicator against the replacement specification.',
      ],
    ],
    example:
      'The hinge on the left mirror is broken. We need the complete power-folding unit with heated glass. ' +
      'Can you quote that version and tell me if we get the indicator and painted cap with it?',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Which part number should you quote? | Parts Relay"
  description="Compare part descriptions and cross-references. Work through position, equipment and kit contents before asking for a quote."
>
  <div class="tool tool-part-details">
    <section class="tool-hero">
      <div class="tool-bound">
        <div class="tool-title">
          <p class="tool-label">Part details</p>
          <h1 tabindex="-1">Which part number should you quote?</h1>
          <p class="tool-intro">
            Two catalogue rows can carry the same description. To choose between them, compare the
            location and equipment with the part on the car.
          </p>
          <div class="page-actions">
            <button type="button" class="page-btn" data-jump="tool-mirror">
              Compare descriptions
            </button>
            <a class="page-btn page-secondary" href="/tools/enquiry-builder/">
              Write an enquiry
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="tool-section">
      <div class="tool-bound">
        <div class="tool-head">
          <p class="tool-label">On the job card</p>
          <h2>Details worth writing down</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-cards" style="--cards: 3">
          <article>
            <div class="tool-glyph">
              <svg
                class="tool-icon"
                viewBox="0 0 32 32"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.45"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="m3 10 13-7 13 7v13l-13 7-13-7zm0 0 13 7 13-7M16 17v13M9 7l13 7" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Extent of the job</h3>
            <p>Will the shop replace one piece, a set, or everything attached to the mount?</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <div class="tool-glyph">
              <svg
                class="tool-icon"
                viewBox="0 0 32 32"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.45"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M16 29S6 18 6 12a10 10 0 1 1 20 0c0 6-10 17-10 17z" />
                <circle cx="16" cy="12" r="3" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Mounting position</h3>
            <p>Which side or axle? Two pieces can look much the same once they’re off the car.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <div class="tool-glyph">
              <svg
                class="tool-icon"
                viewBox="0 0 32 32"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.45"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="m3 22 19-19 7 7-19 19zm5-3 4 4m0-8 3 3m1-7 4 4m0-8 3 3" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Identifying marks</h3>
            <p>
              Copy a legible number from the old unit. Where there’s no number, describe a feature
              the supplier can compare, such as a connector.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <dl class="tool-detail-strip">
          <div>
            <dt>Part</dt>
            <dd>Mirror</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Position</dt>
            <dd>Left</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Feature to check</dt>
            <dd>Heated</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="tool-section tool-muted">
      <div class="tool-bound">
        <div class="tool-columns">
          <div class="tool-head">
            <p class="tool-label">Mirror repairs</p>
            <h2>Left mirror, housing intact</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-feature-cards">
            <article>
              <p>Damage reported</p>
              <h3>Cracked glass</h3>
              <p>
                On some vehicles you can replace the glass on its own. The counter will need to
                check how this one attaches to the existing housing.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <p>Equipment and fit</p>
              <h3>Heated or unheated?</h3>
              <p>
                Have the technician look behind the old glass for heater terminals and identify the
                backing plate. A damaged mount changes the job to a complete assembly.
              </p>
              <dl class="tool-spec">
                <div>
                  <dt>Mounting side</dt>
                  <dd>Left</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Housing</dt>
                  <dd>Retained</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Heating terminals</dt>
                  <dd>Check old glass</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <a class="tool-textlink" href="/tools/enquiry-builder/">
                Prepare a mirror enquiry
              </a>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="tool-section" id="tool-mirror" data-picker tabindex="-1">
      <div class="tool-bound">
        <div class="tool-columns">
          <div>
            <div class="tool-head">
              <p class="tool-label">Quote wording</p>
              <h2>How the enquiry changes if the hinge is broken</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-choices" role="group" aria-label="Choose a mirror component">
              {wordings.map((wording, index) => (
                <button
                  type="button"
                  data-pick={index}
                  aria-pressed={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
                >
                  {wording.label}
                </button>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div data-picker-text aria-live="polite">
            <MirrorWording wording={wordings[0]} />
          </div>
          {wordings.map((wording, index) => (
            <template data-option={index}>
              <MirrorWording wording={wording} />
            </template>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="tool-section tool-muted">
      <div class="tool-bound">
        <div class="tool-head">
          <p class="tool-label">Catalogue results</p>
          <h2>Reading an original number and its cross-references</h2>
          <p class="tool-copy">
            Start in the catalogue section for the assembly. An aftermarket reference, when one
            comes back, points to the original part it matches.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-result-grid">
          <div>
            <dl class="tool-field-notes">
              <div>
                <dt>Original equipment (OE)</dt>
                <dd>
                  Use the manufacturer’s description alongside its code. Copy the spaces and any
                  letters at the end when you send the number to the supplier.
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Aftermarket match</dt>
                <dd>
                  Look for the replacement brand, its part number and description, then read the
                  original code on that row. An empty list means this search didn’t find a
                  cross-reference.
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Before accepting the quote</dt>
                <dd>
                  Compare the proposed replacement with the equipment and markings on the car. Ask
                  the supplier what comes with that reference, what it costs and when the complete
                  order can arrive.
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </div>
          <div
            class="tool-exploded"
            role="img"
            aria-label="Layers of a part description, from vehicle to component, position and fitted equipment"
          >
            <div class="tool-stack">
              <div style="--layer: 0">
                <span>Equipment</span>
              </div>
              <div style="--layer: 1">
                <span>Position</span>
              </div>
              <div style="--layer: 2">
                <span>Component</span>
              </div>
              <div style="--layer: 3">
                <span>Vehicle</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="tool-section">
      <div class="tool-bound">
        <div class="tool-columns">
          <div class="tool-head">
            <p class="tool-label">Details from the vehicle</p>
            <h2>Questions that hold up a quote</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-faq">
            <details name="details-faq">
              <summary>Which side should I give?</summary>
              <p>
                Give left or right from the point of view of someone in the vehicle facing forward.
                Add the mounting position if there’s still room for doubt.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details name="details-faq">
              <summary>What if the number on the old unit is unclear?</summary>
              <p>
                Send the characters you can read and say which ones are unclear. Ask what else on
                the unit would distinguish it.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details name="details-faq">
              <summary>Can I ask about a full assembly?</summary>
              <p>
                Yes. Name the assembly and any fittings or accessories you expect to receive with
                it.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details name="details-faq">
              <summary>Do all requests need every detail?</summary>
              <p>
                Often the vehicle and a clear part name are enough to get started. The counter can
                ask for another detail if more than one version comes up.
              </p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ClosingBand
      title="Put it on the repair order"
      text="Include the mounting side and any identifying marks in your enquiry. A drawing can help if the name on the job card is unclear."
      primary={{ href: '/tools/enquiry-builder/', label: 'Write to your distributor' }}
      secondary={{ href: '/tools/parts-diagrams/', label: 'Browse the drawings' }}
    />
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/picker.js';
</script>
